    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "A style of faulting produced by slip along pre-existing joint zones results in heterogeneous fault zones composed of a peripheral fracture network and a central damaged core. The permeability structure of these fault zones varies with slip magnitude and initial joint zone geometry. In general increasing slip is correlated to decreasing fault normal permeability and increasing fault parallel permeability.",
